# Byte fidelity is a hard requirement for this repo, not a style preference.
#
# The FRA transport binding refuses a session unless several files hash to the
# same SHA-256 on both machines — among them STANDING-ORDERS.md,
# config/standing-orders.json, config/toolsenabled.policy.json and
# config/uac-delegation-allowlist.json. Git's default on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true, set system-wide here) rewrites line endings on both
# checkin and checkout, so the same commit can land on two machines with
# different bytes and therefore different digests. That is the same class of
# failure that produced the 2026-08-02 FRA outage, and it is exactly what this
# repo exists to stop.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion: what was committed is what is
# checked out, on every machine, whatever its local core.autocrlf says.
* -text

# Reviewed public provider artifacts retain exact cross-platform manifest bytes.
/provider-runtimes/gemini-quota/** binary
/tools/provider-runtimes/gemini-quota/** -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
